        "original_id": "530b60d8-745a-56ba-b3a9-b59ed38087a0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Anatole Litvak, Kinji Fukasaku, Olivia de Havilland, Mark Stevens, Leo Genn, Celeste Holm, Beulah Bondi, Lee Patrick\n- Works: The Snake Pit\n- Roles: filmmaker, director, producer, screenwriter, actor\n- Topics: American film, Japanese film, Russian-born artists\n\nFacts:\n- Anatole Litvak was born on May 21, 1902, and he was a Russian-born American filmmaker who wrote, directed, and produced films in various countries and languages.\n- Kinji Fukasaku was born on July 3, 1930, and he was a Japanese film director and screenwriter.\n- The Snake Pit is a 1948 American drama film directed by Anatole Litvak.\n- The Snake Pit stars Olivia de Havilland, Mark Stevens, Leo Genn, Celeste Holm, Beulah Bondi, and Lee Patrick.\n- Anatole Litvak died on December 15, 1974.\n- Kinji Fukasaku died on January 12, 2003.",
